```text
UDC-22-00430
February 6, 2023
RECOMMENDED MOTION:

Move to approve the Back 40 Subdivision, Third Filing Expedited Preliminary Plat, advancing the Final
Plat to the Governing Body, with a recommended exception to block size.

APPLICABLE CITY CODE SECTION(S) AND PLANS:

UDC 2.1.2 Preliminary Plat Approval

UDC 2.1.3 Final Plat Approval

UDC Article 4 Subdivisions

UDC Article 5 Zoning Regulations

PlanCheyenne

BACKGROUND:

The applicant is requesting approval of a plat create multiple lots and a street network for future
development, to include a City-owned parcel and other parcels for commercial or residential development.

SURROUNDING LAND USE AND ZONING:

ANALYSIS OF APPLICATION CONFORMANCE WITH REVIEW CRITERIA:

Should the Planning Commission wish to recommend approval of the Preliminary Plat, the Commission
must make the following findings required in UDC 2.1.2.d   a detailed analysis is below:

1) The application is in accordance with the development policies and physical patterns
identified in the Comprehensive Plan. (UDC 2.1.2.d.1)

The future land use map within PlanCheyenne identifies this area as developing with a mix of
residential and commercial uses, and the proposed plat in the existing zoning districts would be
compatible with this objective. PlanCheyenne supports the use of existing infrastructure and
timely provision of services (including emergency and education services). This development is
proposed in an area which has largely existing infrastructure, although expansion of
infrastructure is necessary for the lots within the site to develop. The property is within the
Urban Service Boundary and has access to all utilities.

